From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:53:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 108/108] v4l2codecs: jpegdec: Report a stream of which no
 image was decoded

Images the driver returned with the error flag, and broken images, were
skipped with gst_video_decoder_drop_frame(). That is the QoS drop, which
marks the decoder as having produced data: a stream of which no image
could be decoded ended with EOS, no frame and no error, and the
application could not tell it from an empty stream.

Release these frames with gst_video_decoder_release_frame() instead.
They still count as decoding errors, so a stream with occasional bad
images carries on as before, while the base class now posts "No valid
frames decoded before end of stream" when no image of the stream could
be decoded.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecjpegdec.c | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecjpegdec.c b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecjpegdec.c
index dbba6b3..09a0c9a 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecjpegdec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecjpegdec.c
@@ -38,8 +38,8 @@
  * caps negotiation, so decodebin and playbin pick a software decoder
  * (jpegdec) for them. What the caps do not show (12-bit samples, Huffman
  * table selectors above 1) is checked on every image and reported as an
- * error; images the driver refuses or cannot finish are dropped with a decode
- * error.
+ * error; images the driver refuses or cannot finish are skipped with a decode
+ * error, and a stream of which no image could be decoded ends with an error.
  *
  * ## Example launch line
  * ```
@@ -732,11 +732,13 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_jpeg_dec_handle_frame (GstVideoDecoder * decoder,
       gst_video_decoder_release_frame (decoder, frame);
       return GST_FLOW_NOT_SUPPORTED;
     }
-    /* Broken image (MJPEG streams have them): drop it. */
+    /* Broken image (MJPEG streams have them): skip it. Release rather
+     * than drop it: a QoS drop counts as decoded data, and a stream of
+     * which no image could be decoded must end with an error. */
     flow_ret = GST_FLOW_OK;
     GST_VIDEO_DECODER_ERROR (self, 1, STREAM, DECODE,
         ("Corrupt JPEG image"), ("%s", reason), flow_ret);
-    gst_video_decoder_drop_frame (decoder, frame);
+    gst_video_decoder_release_frame (decoder, frame);
     return flow_ret;
   }
 
@@ -849,13 +851,15 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_jpeg_dec_handle_frame (GstVideoDecoder * decoder,
 
   if (gst_v4l2_request_has_buf_error (request)) {
     /* The driver refused or could not finish this image (see the kernel
-     * log); a corrupt MJPEG frame should not end the stream. */
+     * log); a corrupt MJPEG frame should not end the stream. Release the
+     * frame rather than drop it, as above: the base class then posts an
+     * error at the end of a stream of which no image was decoded. */
     gst_v4l2_request_unref (request);
     flow_ret = GST_FLOW_OK;
     GST_VIDEO_DECODER_ERROR (self, 1, STREAM, DECODE,
         ("Failed to decode frame %u", frame->system_frame_number),
         ("the driver returned the picture with the error flag"), flow_ret);
-    gst_video_decoder_drop_frame (decoder, frame);
+    gst_video_decoder_release_frame (decoder, frame);
     return flow_ret;
   }
 
